      ],
      "text": "Boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " increased death in elderly patients with dementia-related psychosis treated with antipsychotics. Tardive dyskinesia (potentially irreversible) may develop, and potentially fatal neuroleptic malignant syndrome (hyperpyrexia, rigidity, altered mental status, autonomic instability) has been reported."
     }
    ]
   },
